   As a counter-proposal to what you've already done, I think it would
fit the Nethack model better (though not be as useful or as friendly
to save-files) if eating a wand simply made it so that every so often,
there was a chance of the wand going off inside your stomach, for
its usual effect (modulo the effects of stomach-flesh).

   Eat what? [w]
   This wand of light is crunchy!
   [...]
   You hear a nearby zap. --more--
   You are blinded by a flash of light! --more--
   The jackal flees in terror!

   This wand of opening is crunchy!
   [...]
   You hear a nearby zap. --more--
   OW!  Son of a... --more--
   But wait!... Your medallion begins to glow. --more--
   That was a narrow escape.  Your medallion crumbles to dust. --more--
   Unfortunately, you still have a gaping hole in your torso. --more--
   DYWYPI?

This method gives a nice consistent approach to wand-eating.  (Of 
course, that may not be what you want!)

   Regardless, IMEO there oughta be at least one YAFM associated with
players' eating glass objects.  ("You eat the glass wand.  It does not 
hurt you.")

